{
  "publication_number": "US20230084507A1",
  "title": "Servers, methods and systems for fair and secure vertical federated learning",
  "assignee": "Huawei Cloud Computing Technologies Co Ltd",
  "filing_date": "2022-09-08",
  "publication_date": "2023-03-16",
  "pse": {
    "problem": "The technical limitation is the need for a fair and secure system for vertical federated learning that preserves data privacy, maintains high accuracy, efficiency, security, and can be applied to various machine learning models.",
    "solution_function": "The system performs federated learning, allowing multiple computing systems of different data owners to train a centralized global model without sharing their private data. The system ensures model fairness by training the machine learning model to satisfy a fairness metric. High security is maintained by only allowing entities to obtain model outputs and preventing acquisition of private information. High accuracy and efficiency are achieved through accurate computation and efficient communication. The system can be applied to various machine learning models.",
    "solution_structure": "The system consists of multiple computing systems (data owners) with local datasets, a server that maintains the centralized global model, and a communication network for transmitting information between data owners and the server.",
    "solution_implementation": "Each data owner performs local training of a local model using machine learning algorithms and its respective set of local data. The learnable parameters of the local model are adjusted based on local learned parameter information transmitted to the server, which updates the centralized global model accordingly. The system uses deep learning or other machine learning techniques such as a deep neural network (DNN) for model implementation.",
    "effect": "The solution provides a fair and secure vertical federated learning system that preserves data privacy, maintains high accuracy, efficiency, and can be applied to various machine learning models."
  },
